From 2920c25e498abef06e3c4e88262ead54684fc60d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RenzDolosa <renz@example.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 09:14:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Scanner Recent Activity showing Unmatched despite a
 matched scan

Root cause: the scan_feed view's LEFT JOIN to employees ran under the
querying user's RLS, so scanner-only accounts (access_scope='scanner')
could never see the joined employee row, even for result='matched'
scans. Replaced it with a SECURITY DEFINER RPC (get_scan_feed) gated by
the same permission check scan_proximity_code() already uses.

Also:
- Add test_scan_proximity_code(): same matching logic/permission gate
  as the real scanner, but never inserts into scan_events, so it never
  touches Recent Activity, an employee's scan_logs, or the Scans count.
- Replace the Employee Manager sidebar's 'Scanner' item with 'Test
  Scan', rendered in-shell (no more window.open on click) using the
  new non-logging RPC. The real, logging scanner is still reachable via
  an 'Open live scanner' link on that page.
- scanner.css: use 100dvh/100dvw for the standalone scanner, a
  3-column grid (spacer/main/feed) so the tap-card hero and search box
  are actually centered on screen instead of skewed left by the feed
  sidebar, and cap Recent Activity to calc(100dvh - ...) with
  overflow-y:auto instead of growing unbounded.
